course: dictionary
lesson: 10249
title: Tomboy and fair words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tomboy is a girl who likes things people used to think were only for boys, such as climbing trees, rough games and football. She often likes jeans more than dresses. «One teacher told Maddie she "can't help it, she's a tomboy", as if liking football meant she was bound to fight.»
explain: Look at the clue: «as if liking football meant she was bound to fight». The words "as if" show that the idea is not true. Liking football does not mean a girl must fight. So the sentence tells us the teacher's idea is unfair, not that Maddie has done anything wrong.
explain: Tomboy describes what a girl likes, not whether she is good or bad. Some older books used the word as a criticism of girls who did not behave in a "ladylike" way. That is the dated meaning, and we do not use it that way now.
explain: When you read a word, ask what the sentence says about the person, and whether the writer thinks it is fair. The context often tells you the answer.
fact: A tomboy is a girl who likes activities people once thought were only for boys, such as climbing trees and football.
fact: «Tomboy» describes what a girl likes, not whether she is good or bad.
fact: In the past, the word was sometimes used as a criticism; that meaning is now dated.
fact: Today we know that girls and boys may like any games, clothes and hobbies.
fact: «A real tomboy» is a girl who really enjoys rough games and climbing.
exercise: What is a tomboy? | A boy who likes ballet | A teacher who runs the football club | A girl who only wears dresses and never plays outside | *A girl who likes climbing trees, rough games and football
exercise: In «as if liking football meant she was bound to fight», what do the words "as if" show? | The teacher is right about Maddie | Maddie likes to fight | The teacher is very happy | *The teacher's idea is unfair
exercise: Which statement is true today? | A girl who likes football must be a bad girl | Only boys may like football | *Girls and boys may like any games, clothes and hobbies | A tomboy should try to be ladylike
test: Maddie likes football and wears jeans to school. What is she? | A ladylike girl | A teacher | A quiet bookworm | *A tomboy
test: What did the dated meaning of tomboy show? | It was a prize for the best football player | *It was once a criticism of girls who were not ladylike | It meant a boy who likes dresses | It meant a girl who never goes outside
exam: Why did the writer put «as if» into the teacher's sentence? | To show that football is dangerous | *To show that the teacher's idea about tomboys is wrong | To show that Maddie really will fight | To show the teacher is very happy
